From: SteveDeFacto <5148995+SteveDeFacto@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 23 Oct 2026 03:32:41 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] sia_storage unit-test harness and two test-only call fixes

- The vendored sia_storage's own unit tests did not compile: two test calls in app_client/http.rs predate the C2
  third argument of delete_object/pin_object. Each now passes None. Test code only (cfg(test)).
- unit/make-manifest.py + unit-step.sh run those tests offline, on the vendored sources, with feature "mock":
  - the manifest is derived from sia_storage's, dropping only the bench and the uncached bench/example
    dev-dependencies;
  - the path dependencies are mirrored with their [[bench]] stanza removed.
- wasm-step.sh / cargo-step.sh are copies of the candidate's. repro-step.sh rebuilds the local crates for the provenance
  check.
- qrun.sh retries a not-started queue job.
- negctl/make.py builds the negative-control vendor tree: the baseline download.rs plus this tree's new tests.
